.TH SNAKE 1 snake
.SH NAME
snake \- terminal snake game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snake
.RB [ \-afn ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR W x H ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR MS ]
.br
.B snake \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
Steer the snake to the food
.RB ( <> ).
Each piece of food makes it one cell longer, scores a point and makes
it a little faster. The game ends when the snake runs into a wall or
into itself, and is won when it fills the whole board.
.PP
The board fills the terminal unless
.B \-s
is given. The game waits for the first direction key. A change of the
terminal size pauses it; when the terminal is smaller than the board,
it says so until it is big enough again.
.B r
starts a new game sized to the terminal as it is then.
.SS Autopilot
With
.B \-a
or
.BR a ,
the game plays itself: it goes at the food on the slant, in a
staircase with steps two cells long, never hits anything, and always
wins. Its way is always part of a Hamiltonian cycle through every
cell, made of 2x2 blocks round a tree, that the whole snake lies on
in order, so it can never be trapped; at each step it looks for such
a cycle that agrees with the body and the way to the food.
.PP
A direction key takes over; with
.B a
the autopilot takes over again, first steering until the snake fits a
cycle, so then a win is likely but not certain. Games it played any
part of do not count for the best score. The cycles need both sides
even, so an odd side is made one cell shorter.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
autopilot from the start
.TP
.BI \-s " W" x H
a board of
.I W
by
.I H
cells (at least 10x6, an odd side made one shorter); a cell is two
columns wide
.TP
.BI \-t " MS"
milliseconds per step at the start (20 to 2000, default 150); each
piece of food takes 2 off, down to 60
.TP
.B \-f
fixed speed: no speed-up when eating
.TP
.B \-n
neither read nor write the best score
.TP
.B \-h
help
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR h " " j " " k " " l ", arrows"
left, down, up, right; two turns can wait for the next steps. With the
autopilot on, you take over.
.TP
.B a
autopilot on and off
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
faster, slower: halves or doubles the time per step (0 to 2000 ms);
after that, eating no longer speeds up
.TP
.BR p ", space"
pause and go on (a direction key goes on too)
.TP
.B r
new game
.TP
.BR q ", Ctrl-c"
quit
.TP
.B Ctrl-z
stop; after
.B fg
the game is paused
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.system/state/snake/best
the best score, one number. It is only kept when
.I ~/.system/state
exists; delete it to start over.
.SH NOTES
Needs a terminal with 256 colours and DEC line drawing (st, xterm,
tmux). It needs nothing but the kernel: a static binary, no curses,
no terminfo.
